id: frozen
name: Frozen
kind: battlefield
envQuality: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Ice underfoot. 4(bT) Ki Points at the start and end of your turn, and moving on it is
  either slow or a Qualified Acrobatics Check away from going over.
text: >
  Frozen: If you start or end your Turn in this Battle Environment, reduce your Ki Points
  by 4(bT). If you use the Movement Maneuver, either halve your Speed for the duration of
  that Maneuver or make an Acrobatics Skill Check with a Difficulty of Qualified. If you
  succeed, nothing happens. If you fail, you are knocked Prone instead (regain the Action
  and any Ki Points spent on this Maneuver).

---

# Ki rather than Life, which is what separates this from Electrified beside it - and 4(bT)
# rather than 2, because Ki is cheaper to lose and there is more of it.
#
# --- The Movement Maneuver, which is the table's ------------------------------------------------
#
# "Either halve your Speed for the duration of that Maneuver or make an Acrobatics Skill
# Check with a Difficulty of Qualified."
#
# A choice the player makes each time they move, and this system has no Movement Maneuver
# to hang it on - `movement` is a Slot written, said and not enforced, because nothing here
# moves anybody. So the choice is the table's: halve the Speed for that move, or roll
# Acrobatics against Qualified from the sheet and take the Prone on a failure.
#
# The failure hands the Action and the Ki back, which is the unusual half and the half
# worth having written down: a Movement Maneuver that puts you on your back costs nothing.
#
# The Difficulty is one the system already knows - Qualified is a Target Number of 14 - so
# the Acrobatics Check rolled from the Skills tab against that Difficulty is the Check the
# rule asks for, with nothing to build.

[automatic/start-of-turn]
ki.value -= 4(bT);

[automatic/end-of-turn]
ki.value -= 4(bT);
